  "points": [
    {
      "debateScope": "general",
      "bio": "W000821",
      "speaker": "Bruce Westerman",
      "side": "Yea",
      "manager": true,
      "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm",
      "start": 6923,
      "quote": "Crucially, this bill upholds strong environmental standards by \nstipulating that Federal requirements may only be waived if operators \nreceive drilling permits and comply with historic preservation laws on \nthe State level.\n  Notably, the bill would not impact the royalties paid to the Federal \nGovernment. Therefore, it will not reduce the Federal revenues \ngenerated by geothermal production.",
      "display": "Crucially, this bill upholds strong environmental standards by stipulating that Federal requirements may only be waived if operators receive drilling permits and comply with historic preservation laws on the State level. Notably, the bill would not impact the royalties paid to the Federal Government. Therefore, it will not reduce the Federal revenues generated by geothermal production.",
      "passageUrl": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm#:~:text=Crucially%2C%20this%20bill%20upholds%20strong%20environmental%20standards%20by%20stipulating%20that%20Federal%20requirements%20may%20only%20be%20waived%20if%20operators%20receive%20drilling%20permits%20and%20comply%20with%20historic%20preservation%20laws%20on%20the%20State%20level.%20Notably%2C%20the%20bill%20would%20not%20impact%20the%20royalties%20paid%20to%20the%20Federal%20Government.%20Therefore%2C%20it%20will%20not%20reduce%20the%20Federal%20revenues%20generated%20by%20geothermal%20production.",
      "end": 7318,
      "sentenceIds": [
        "2.10",
        "2.11",
        "2.12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "debateScope": "general",
      "bio": "K000397",
      "speaker": "Young Kim",
      "side": "Yea",
      "manager": false,
      "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm",
      "start": 16269,
      "quote": "The HEATS Act fixes that by cutting red tape and waiving Federal \ndrilling permit requirements for geothermal wells on State and local \nlands. Operators will still go through a rigorous State-level \npermitting process, but they will no longer be subjected to duplicative \nFederal requirements that slow production, raise costs, and kill jobs.",
      "display": "The HEATS Act fixes that by cutting red tape and waiving Federal drilling permit requirements for geothermal wells on State and local lands. Operators will still go through a rigorous State-level permitting process, but they will no longer be subjected to duplicative Federal requirements that slow production, raise costs, and kill jobs.",
      "passageUrl": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm#:~:text=The%20HEATS%20Act%20fixes%20that%20by%20cutting%20red%20tape%20and%20waiving%20Federal%20drilling%20permit%20requirements%20for%20geothermal%20wells%20on%20State%20and%20local%20lands.%20Operators%20will%20still%20go%20through%20a%20rigorous%20State%2Dlevel%20permitting%20process%2C%20but%20they%20will%20no%20longer%20be%20subjected%20to%20duplicative%20Federal%20requirements%20that%20slow%20production%2C%20raise%20costs%2C%20and%20kill%20jobs.",
      "end": 16611,
      "sentenceIds": [
        "6.6",
        "6.7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "debateScope": "general",
      "bio": "A000381",
      "speaker": "Yassamin Ansari",
      "side": "Nay",
      "manager": true,
      "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm",
      "start": 25312,
      "quote": "Mr. Speaker, in closing, even good energy sources need good \npermitting policy. I am a strong supporter of geothermal energy, but \nthe HEATS Act could undermine the on-the-ground support and good \nenvironmental track record geothermal currently enjoys.",
      "display": "in closing, even good energy sources need good permitting policy. I am a strong supporter of geothermal energy, but the HEATS Act could undermine the on-the-ground support and good environmental track record geothermal currently enjoys.",
      "passageUrl": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm#:~:text=Mr.%20Speaker%2C%20in%20closing%2C%20even%20good%20energy%20sources%20need%20good%20permitting%20policy.%20I%20am%20a%20strong%20supporter%20of%20geothermal%20energy%2C%20but%20the%20HEATS%20Act%20could%20undermine%20the%20on%2Dthe%2Dground%20support%20and%20good%20environmental%20track%20record%20geothermal%20currently%20enjoys.",
      "end": 25564,
      "sentenceIds": [
        "10.1",
        "10.2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "debateScope": "general",
      "bio": "H001068",
      "speaker": "Jared Huffman",
      "side": "Nay",
      "manager": false,
      "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm",
      "start": 18928,
      "quote": "While this may sound innocuous--oh, it is just subsurface; it is \nbelow what we can see with our eyes--without a Federal permit, the core \nsafeguards for development affecting Federal resources would totally \ndisappear. That includes protections under the National Environmental \nPolicy Act, the National Historic Preservation Act, and the Endangered \nSpecies Act.",
      "display": "While this may sound innocuous--oh, it is just subsurface; it is below what we can see with our eyes--without a Federal permit, the core safeguards for development affecting Federal resources would totally disappear. That includes protections under the National Environmental Policy Act, the National Historic Preservation Act, and the Endangered Species Act.",
      "passageUrl": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CREC-2026-04-23/html/CREC-2026-04-23-pt1-PgH3073-4.htm#:~:text=While%20this%20may%20sound%20innocuous%2D%2Doh%2C%20it%20is%20just%20subsurface%3B%20it%20is%20below%20what%20we%20can%20see%20with%20our%20eyes%2D%2Dwithout%20a%20Federal%20permit%2C%20the%20core%20safeguards%20for%20development%20affecting%20Federal%20resources%20would%20totally%20disappear.%20That%20includes%20protections%20under%20the%20National%20Environmental%20Policy%20Act%2C%20the%20National%20Historic%20Preservation%20Act%2C%20and%20the%20Endangered%20Species%20Act.",
      "end": 19292,
      "sentenceIds": [
        "8.11",
        "8.12"
      ]
    }
